window.docContents[217].resolve({"/Elementary-Functions/___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions--___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions--Principal-values":{"contents":"Source: DLMF §4.37(ii)\n\nE7–E9 are the principal reciprocal branches; E7 and E8 exclude zero, while E9\nalso excludes its stated poles. The six panels of Figure 4.37.1\nshow the cuts for the three basic functions and their reciprocals. Graphs for\nreal arguments appear in §4.29, while the same\nsection points to conformal mappings and complex surface plots.\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions\u0009§4.37 Inverse Hyperbolic Functions\u0009§4.37 Inverse Hyperbolic Functions","header":"Principal values","id":"/Elementary-Functions/___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions--___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions--Principal-values"},"/Elementary-Functions/___4___7-Derivatives-and-Differential-Equations/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___7-Derivatives-and-Differential-Equations--___4___7-Derivatives-and-Differential-Equations":{"contents":"This section follows the two DLMF subsections: logarithms, then exponentials and\npowers.  Complex formulas use Mathlib's principal Complex.log, Complex.exp,\nand Complex.cpow; where DLMF discusses an arbitrary branch or a general\nsolution, the branch, antiderivative, or constants are explicit parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions\u0009§4.7 Derivatives and Differential Equations","header":"§4.7 Derivatives and Differential Equations","id":"/Elementary-Functions/___4___7-Derivatives-and-Differential-Equations/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___7-Derivatives-and-Differential-Equations--___4___7-Derivatives-and-Differential-Equations"}});